{"id":"AR-state_setback_standard-1","technology":"wind","policy_type":"state_setback_standard","who_decides":"state_board","state_body":"Arkansas Public Service Commission","threshold_mw":"wind:5","summary":"To get a state permit, each turbine must sit at least the greater of 3.5 times its tip height or 2,500 feet from a nonparticipating property line (waivable to 1.1 times height) and one mile from schools, hospitals, nursing homes, churches, city or town limits, state or federal parks and public airports; noise may not exceed 35 dBA at a nonparticipating dwelling or 45 dBA at the property line, and shadow flicker is capped at 30 hours a year. Local wind rules may be stricter but not less restrictive.","statute_citation":"Ark. Code 23-18-1406 (2025 Ark. Acts 945, sec. 1, enacted as 23-18-1306(a),(b)(2)(B)(vi),(c)); 23-18-1413 (enacted as 23-18-1313(a)(2))","statute_url":"https://arkleg.state.ar.us/Acts/FTPDocument?path=%2FACTS%2F2025R%2FPublic%2F&file=945.pdf&ddBienniumSession=2025%2F2025R","evidence_level":"primary_source","verification":"verified","reviewed_on":"2026-10-09"}
